<% prose = "mt-3 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400" %>
<% step = "mt-12 text-lg font-semibold" %>

<p class="<%= prose %>">
  Three pieces, used together: the form mints the record's id, the page draws the record under that id as it
  submits, and the server's element replaces the drawing because it has the same id. Nothing is matched up
  by hand, and nothing shows twice.
</p>

<h2 class="<%= step %>">1. Mint the id in the form</h2>
<p class="<%= prose %>">
  <code>uuid_field</code> is a hidden field holding a fresh UUIDv7, minted in the browser and again whenever
  the form resets. Without the script, the server's own id is sent.
</p>
<% optimistic_uuid_source = capture do %><%%= form.uuid_field :id %><% end %>
<div class="mt-4"><%= render "code", id: "optimistic_uuid", source: optimistic_uuid_source.to_str %></div>

<h2 class="<%= step %>">2. Draw the submission</h2>
<p class="<%= prose %>">
  <code>&lt;unmagic-optimistic&gt;</code>, inside the form, clones its template on submit. It takes the
  element's id and text from the form's fields and places it in <code>container</code>.
</p>
<% optimistic_source = capture do %><%%= form_with model: Comment.new, builder: Unmagic::Components::FormBuilder do |form| %>
  <%%= form.uuid_field :id %>
  <unmagic-optimistic container="#comments">
    <%%= form.text_area :body, required: true %>
    <template>
      <article class="comment is-pending" data-optimistic-id="comment[id]">
        <p data-optimistic-text="comment[body]"></p>
      </article>
    </template>
  </unmagic-optimistic>
  <%%= form.submit "Comment" %>
<%% end %><% end %>
<div class="mt-4"><%= render "code", id: "optimistic_form", source: optimistic_source.to_str %></div>
<p class="<%= prose %>">
  A required field stops an empty form from submitting, so there's never a drawing with no record coming for
  it. <code>scroll="false"</code> stops the new element scrolling into view.
</p>

<h2 class="<%= step %>">3. Answer with the real element</h2>
<p class="<%= prose %>">
  Create the record with the submitted id and answer with an
  <%= link_to "upsert", guide_path("turbo_streams"), class: "underline" %>, from the response or a broadcast.
  The element with that id is already on the page, so it's replaced in place:
</p>
<div class="mt-4">
  <%= render "code", id: "optimistic_controller", language: :ruby, source: <<~'RUBY'.strip %>
    def create
      @comment = Comment.create!(params.expect(comment: %i[id body]))
      render turbo_stream: turbo_stream.action(:upsert, "comments", @comment)
    end
  RUBY
</div>
<p class="<%= prose %>">
  <code>ai_chat_composer</code> does all of this for chat. Needs <code>import "unmagic/components/uuid_input"</code>,
  <code>"unmagic/components/optimistic"</code> and <code>"unmagic/components/upsert"</code>.
</p>
